  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "A capacitor of capacitance $C_{0}$ is charged to a potential $V_{0}$ and is connected with another capacitor of capacitance $C$ as shown. After closing the switch $S,$ the common potential across the two capacitors becomes $V$. The capacitance $C$ is given by <img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/wbjee/2013_phy_q24.png\">",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "AOcHE",
      "text": "$\\frac{C_{0}\\left(V_{0}-h\\right)}{V_{0}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "ecIxE",
      "text": "$\\frac{C_{0}\\left(V-V_{0}\\right)}{V_{0}}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "jZyYh",
      "text": "$\\frac{C_{0}\\left(V+V_{0}\\right)}{V}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "y6pwc",
      "text": "$\\frac{C_{0}\\left(V_{0}-V\\right)}{V}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "When the switch $S$ is closed, the common potential across the two capacitors becomes $V$. so charge on isolated plates remains same.\r\n$$\r\n\\begin{array}{lr}\r\n\\therefore \\quad C_{0} V_{0}=\\left(C_{0}+C\\right)V \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow \\quad C V=C_{0} V_{0}-C_{0} V \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow \\quad C=\\frac{C_{0}\\left(V_{0}-V\\right)}{V}\r\n\\end{array}\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
